<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Kel Ajjer</h1><p class="st-meta">1660 CE – 1916 CE (approx.) · capital Ghat</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Tuareg confederation of the Tassili n'Ajjer, based around the oasis of Ghat, which controlled caravan routes between Libya and the Sahel.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Kel Ajjer emerged as a distinct confederation of the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tuareg">Tuareg</a>, occupying the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tassili-najjer">Tassili n'Ajjer</a> plateau and the oases of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghat">Ghat</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/djanet">Djanet</a> in present-day south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a> and south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/libya">Libya</a>. Their organisation took shape by the 17th century.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The confederation was led by an amenokal from a noble lineage, presiding over noble warriors, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> herders and dependent oasis farmers. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghat">Ghat</a> was a key stop on the caravan route from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-tripoli">Tripoli</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kano">Kano</a>, and the Kel Ajjer taxed and protected caravans. They fought a long war with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kel-ahaggar">Kel Ahaggar</a> in the 1870s.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> garrisoned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghat">Ghat</a> from 1875, and later <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/italian-libya">Italian Libya</a> claimed it, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/djanet">Djanet</a> in 1911. Many Kel Ajjer joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/senussi-order">Senussi Order</a>'s revolt against the French in 1916, which was suppressed, dividing the confederation between French and Italian rule.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 1660 CE – 1916 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:92.74%;width:5.09%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1660 CE – 1916 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>nomadic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Ghat</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Tamahaq (Tuareg)</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/algeria">Algeria</a>, <a href="/countries/libya">Libya</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kel Ajjer confederation, Ajjer Tuareg</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1788&amp;focus=kel-ajjer" aria-label="Kel Ajjer on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4950 1259 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kel Ajjer lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5270 1515L5077 1108"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5077 1108h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5270 1515h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5270 1515h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Ghat. <a href="/atlas?year=1788&amp;focus=kel-ajjer">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

